{
  "notes": [
    "Every vector is H_FIELDS_V1 over exactly two fields: u32_be(leaf_version) and canonical_leaf_bytes.",
    "canonical_leaf_bytes is a single nested FRAME_V1 over 25 fields and does not itself contain leaf_version. An implementation that promotes the 25 fields to outer fields, or hashes protobuf marshal bytes, produces a different digest.",
    "The two optional ratios encode presence in band: absent is the single byte 0x00, present is 0x01 followed by the framed uint32. Their presence is decided solely by the locked profile's compare flags, so the two vectors below are two profiles, not two token states.",
    "worker_logprob_fp_1e6, verifier_logprob_fp_1e6 and rank_delta are int64 in two's complement; abs_logprob_diff_fp_1e6 is uint64. rank_delta equals verifier_rank minus worker_rank, with rank 0 meaning outside the required top-k.",
    "leaf_hashes feed MerkleRoot(\"TRUEOPEN_PREFILL_TOKEN_METRIC_ROOT_V2\", ...) in output_position order, contiguous from 0 and unique.",
    "Each vector carries mutations[]: one per encodable leaf plus the semantic cases §10.1 names. A mutation only asserts the digest moves or the input is rejected; it never introduces a domain. digest_hex is the value the mutated input produces, so an implementation that ignores a field will reproduce the positive digest and fail here.",
    "Each vector carries mutations[]: one per encodable leaf plus the semantic cases §10.1 names. A mutation only asserts the digest moves or the input is rejected; it never introduces a domain. digest_hex is the value the mutated input produces, so an implementation that ignores a field will reproduce the positive digest and fail here.",
    "Each vector carries mutations[]: one per encodable leaf plus the semantic cases §10.1 names. A mutation only asserts the digest moves or the input is rejected; it never introduces a domain. digest_hex is the value the mutated input produces, so an implementation that ignores a field will reproduce the positive digest and fail here."
  ],
